_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Prevent parallel reconnect timers from creating overlapping reconnect attempts.**

`_scheduleReconnect()` does not guard against an already scheduled timer, so repeated close/error paths can queue multiple reconnects concurrently.


<details>
<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 _scheduleReconnect() {
+    if (this.reconnectTimer) {
+        return; // reconnect already scheduled
+    }
     if (this.reconnectAttempts >= this.options.maxReconnectAttempts) {
         console.error('[WebSocket] Max reconnection attempts reached');
         return;
     }
@@
-    this.reconnectTimer = setTimeout(() => {
+    this.reconnectTimer = setTimeout(() => {
+        this.reconnectTimer = null;
         this.reconnectAttempts++;
         this.connect();
     }, delay);
 }
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@gui/static/websocket_client.js` around lines 284 - 297, _scheduleReconnect
currently allows multiple timers to be scheduled concurrently which can cause
overlapping connect() calls; before scheduling a new timer, check if
this.reconnectTimer is already set and if so return (or clear it first), then
assign the setTimeout to this.reconnectTimer, and ensure the timeout handler
clears this.reconnectTimer (set to null) after firing and before calling
this.connect() and incrementing this.reconnectAttempts; use the existing symbols
_scheduleReconnect, this.reconnectTimer, this.reconnectAttempts,
this.options.maxReconnectAttempts, and this.connect to implement this guard.
```

</details>

